body:
Coordinator, merge note for head dd216d57c6cd09cf5680a4e3198f9a6aca4980ce. Class: DELTA and new code, both reviewed (the delta review marker on this head). I set `merge-ready` and flag the PR ready now. Nothing is pushed after this.

The maintainer decision of 2026-11-22 on this PR: "merge after the refresh, a delta read and a green trial merge with current `main`." The three are done:
- the refresh: the merges of `main` and the commits by the maintainers (the note routing, the two goldens, the `G73` / `G85` dwell refusal, the axis inversion note, the arc guard);
- the reads: the review of 783b33f6f and the delta review of dd216d57c, no blocker;
- the trial merge on `main` 35940da16 (the merge is clean): 62 gate steps, 0 failed:
  - post: the lib 96, `script_mach3` 11, `coincident_arcs` 8, `comment_escape` 4, `g73_g85_dwell_linuxcnc` 9, `wcs_flip_dialects` 9, `upright_after_tilt` 13, `radius_arcs` 7, `fanuc_post` 12, `recorded_streams` 12 and five more;
  - app: `conformance` 7, `posting` 17, `golden_cl` 33, `first_part_programs` 2, the three example catalog suites, `post_serves_kind` 6, `program_units` 7, `program_entry` 9, `explain_option` 4, `smoothing` 7, `per_op_files` 9, `coolant*`, `machine_library` 16, `shipped_from_disk` 3 and others (29 steps);
  - the app lib 298 and the ui lib 1477 (8 ignored);
  - clippy on `camcraft-post` with all targets and on the `camcraft-app` lib: clean. No golden changed in the run.
- On the head before it: the whole post crate (125 binaries, 1026 tests).

Not run: the other steps of the quick plan (793 steps), and the heavy lanes (not a merge condition, #3556).

It is a `feat`: it merges when it is reviewed and gated.

@HansFel thank you for the Mach3 post. Follow-ups are in #3530 (Explain G-code, the `G86` dwell, the millisecond dwell test, a `mach3_builtin` test) and #3565 (the repeated tool).
